/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 252 0 R
/E (The reduced dataset achieved higher accuracy across all tests, indicating that attribute reduction improved model performance. This improvement occurred because irrelevant and redundant attributes were removed, allowing the decision tree to focus on the most significant features influencing customer churn, such as tenure, contract type, online security, technical support, and payment method. As a result, noise and overfitting were reduced, leading to better generalization. Among all evaluation methods, the 80:20 percentage split produced the highest accuracy due to the larger training dataset, which enabled the model to learn more representative customer behaviour patterns while maintaining sufficient data for reliable testing.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [1]
>>
